Forward Contracts (Regulation) Act, 1952
(n)
the regulation of fluctuations in rates and prices;
(o)
the emergencies in trade which may arise and the exercise of powers in such emergencies including the power to fix
maximum and minimum prices;
(p)
the regulation of dealings by members for their own account;
(q)
the limitations on the volume of trade done by any individual member;
